WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:04:20.611 --> 00:04:24.198
There's simply no way to shield
against every weaponized agent.

3
00:04:24.281 --> 00:04:26.200
Instead. I can make
super-immune systems...

4
00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:28.953
by strengthening
the human cellular response.

5
00:04:28.994 --> 00:04:30.955
Banner. I know
where you're going.

6
00:04:30.996 --> 00:04:33.207
But manipulating the immune system
is dangerous and stupid.

7
00:04:33.249 --> 00:04:37.211
The president's science advisors
made it absolutely clear...

8
00:04:37.294 --> 00:04:40.297
no human subjects.

9
00:05:02.361 --> 00:05:04.405
David. I have wonderful news.

10
00:05:07.408 --> 00:05:09.577
I'm gonna have a baby.

11
00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:53.347
What's it gonna be?  Whoa. look at that.
Bruce. Huh?  Want a dinosaur?

12
00:06:53.431 --> 00:06:55.933
Let's have a little fight.

13
00:06:56.017 --> 00:06:58.352
You don't scare me.

14
00:07:00.438 --> 00:07:03.649
That's a delicious eyeball.  Ooh. you're big
and green and scary.  I'm gonna run away.

15
00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.845
Really. speaking of Cheryl.
guess what...

16
00:07:32.928 --> 00:07:34.889
Bruce. you're hurt!

17
00:07:36.098 --> 00:07:39.143
Jack hit him with the stick.
but Bruce wouldn't hit him back.

18
00:07:39.226 --> 00:07:41.729
He just stood there. shaking.

19
00:07:41.812 --> 00:07:43.814
It's okay.

20
00:07:50.863 --> 00:07:52.782
Yeah. strange
he didn't make a peep.

21
00:07:52.865 --> 00:07:55.326
Any other kid
would've wailed his head off.

22
00:07:55.409 --> 00:07:56.994
That's Bruce. He's like that.

23
00:07:57.036 --> 00:07:59.663
He's just so... bottled up.

24
00:08:03.918 --> 00:08:06.879
The samples we found in your lab...
they were human blood.

25
00:08:06.921 --> 00:08:08.881
You've ignored protocol.

26
00:08:08.923 --> 00:08:11.675
You had no right
snooping around in my lab.

27
00:08:11.801 --> 00:08:13.719
That's my business.

28
00:08:13.844 --> 00:08:17.765
Wrong. Banner.  It's government business.
and you're off the project.

29
00:08:39.829 --> 00:08:42.707
Attention. all personnel.
Fail-safe has been initiated.

30
00:08:42.748 --> 00:08:45.418
Gamma decontamination
will occur in 30 minutes!

31
00:08:45.501 --> 00:08:47.169
Evacuate immediately!

32
00:08:47.253 --> 00:08:49.547
I repeat. evacuate immediately!

33
00:09:08.816 --> 00:09:11.777
- Edith?
- David. what's going on?

34
00:09:11.861 --> 00:09:15.031
- I gotta talk to you. Edith.
- Bruce. stay here.

35
00:09:17.158 --> 00:09:19.118
What are you doing?

36
00:09:52.234 --> 00:09:54.153
What are you doing?

37
00:09:54.236 --> 00:09:57.156
I'm trying to tell you
what has to be done!

38
00:09:57.239 --> 00:09:59.700
David. please stop it!
No!

39
00:10:04.872 --> 00:10:06.874
No! No!
Yes!

40
00:10:06.916 --> 00:10:09.377
David! No!

41
00:10:15.966 --> 00:10:18.344
Bruce.

42
00:10:18.386 --> 00:10:20.388
Bruce. wake up. son.

43
00:10:20.388 --> 00:10:23.432
Bruce. Bruce.

44
00:10:26.727 --> 00:10:29.271
Another nightmare?

45
00:10:29.355 --> 00:10:31.816
I don't know.

46
00:10:31.857 --> 00:10:33.984
I don't remember.

47
00:10:35.528 --> 00:10:37.530
Hi. Mom.

48
00:10:38.906 --> 00:10:41.867
Already off to college.

49
00:10:41.909 --> 00:10:43.869
Gonna miss you terribly.

50
00:10:43.911 --> 00:10:45.871
I'll miss you too.

51
00:10:45.913 --> 00:10:47.957
Please. come here.

52
00:10:49.417 --> 00:10:51.877
Look at you.

53
00:10:52.002 --> 00:10:55.047
Soon to be a great scientist.

54
00:10:55.089 --> 00:10:56.924
I guess.

55
00:10:57.007 --> 00:10:58.968
- I mean. who knows?
- I do.

56
00:10:59.009 --> 00:11:03.222
There's something inside you...
so special.

57
00:11:04.265 --> 00:11:06.225
Some kind of greatness.

58
00:11:06.267 --> 00:11:08.394
I'm sure someday you're gonna...

59
00:11:08.436 --> 00:11:10.855
share it with the whole world.

60
00:12:05.368 --> 00:12:08.621
But as far as I'm concerned.
security oughta be...

61
00:12:09.038 --> 00:12:10.623
Good morning. Dr. Krenzler.

62
00:12:10.748 --> 00:12:14.585
Security oughta be beefed up.  In a
place like this you can't be too careful

63
00:12:14.668 --> 00:12:16.921
Bruce!  Big day.

64
00:12:17.004 --> 00:12:19.965
- Did you sleep?  I didn't sleep.
- I slept okay.

65
00:12:20.049 --> 00:12:22.426
- Is Betty here?
- She's around.

66
00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:25.638
I really gotta say. seeing you
in that stylin' head wear...

67
00:12:25.721 --> 00:12:28.933
You're implying something
about my helmet?

68
00:12:29.058 --> 00:12:32.019
You look like a massive nerd.
even around other scientists.

69
00:12:32.144 --> 00:12:36.357
Can I just ask... Were you wearing
the helmet while she dumped you?

70
00:12:36.357 --> 00:12:38.859
See. it protects my very
important brain. Harper.

71
00:12:38.901 --> 00:12:41.028
Go prep the samples.

72
00:12:42.029 --> 00:12:45.491
- Hey. I found you.
- Betty. hey.

73
00:12:48.828 --> 00:12:50.955
I hate them.

74
00:12:51.038 --> 00:12:53.332
-Wait. I just got here.  Who do we hate?
-The review board.

75
00:12:53.416 --> 00:12:56.335
We have to make a
presentation on Tuesday.

76
00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.504
And you're gonna make it with me.

77
00:12:58.546 --> 00:13:00.715
You think I should?

78
00:13:00.923 --> 00:13:03.259
Yeah. you're great with that stuff.

79
00:13:03.259 --> 00:13:08.472
You start talking about microbes and
nanomeds. you sound almost... passionate

80
00:13:10.641 --> 00:13:13.060
I'm sorry.

81
00:13:13.102 --> 00:13:15.187
That was rude.

82
00:13:15.271 --> 00:13:17.732
Look. nobody expects this
to be easy.

83
00:13:17.773 --> 00:13:21.027
us working together
after being... so close.

84
00:13:21.068 --> 00:13:23.029
We were close?

85
00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.448
Look. if I could be more...

86
00:13:27.408 --> 00:13:29.368
whatever. you know...

87
00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:31.620
- I'm... just...
- Don't.

88
00:13:31.704 --> 00:13:34.081
It's not your fault. really.

89
00:13:34.165 --> 00:13:36.083
You're just a by-product...

90
00:13:36.167 --> 00:13:39.128
of my inexplicable obsession
with emotionally distant men.

91
00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.213
I'll get over us.

92
00:13:42.214 --> 00:13:44.216
Good for you.

93
00:13:44.258 --> 00:13:47.219
Anyway. I'm just really stressed
about this review.

94
00:13:47.303 --> 00:13:51.432
If we don't get impressive results today.
we're gonna have a really hard sell come Tuesday.

95
00:13:52.808 --> 00:13:54.769
Well. then. let's go be impressive.

96
00:14:38.688 --> 00:14:40.648
Harper?

97
00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.567
Ready when you are.
Let's hit it.

98
00:14:48.489 --> 00:14:50.282
Are we passing inspection?

99
00:14:50.408 --> 00:14:52.785
Safeties all going green.

100
00:14:52.827 --> 00:14:54.829
Countdown's started.

101
00:14:57.748 --> 00:14:59.959
Nanomeds released.

102
00:15:02.044 --> 00:15:04.004
Four seconds.

103
00:15:07.174 --> 00:15:09.844
Okay. nanomeds fully dispersed.

104
00:15:11.345 --> 00:15:15.182
Okay. let's hit Freddie
with the gamma radiation.

105
00:15:28.237 --> 00:15:30.197
Gamma exposure.

106
00:15:32.283 --> 00:15:33.993
Nanomeds now active.

107
00:15:37.204 --> 00:15:40.958
Nanomeds replicating cells on border.

108
00:15:41.042 --> 00:15:43.002
It's working.

109
00:15:46.547 --> 00:15:50.384
Cell copy to disassemble ratio
holding within one percent.

110
00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.394
Imbalanced nanomed activity.

111
00:16:12.615 --> 00:16:15.159
You wanna go to the review board
on Monday and tell 'em...

112
00:16:15.159 --> 00:16:18.204
we've developed a brand-new
method for exploding frogs?

113
00:16:18.245 --> 00:16:21.540
Yeah. I think maybe
there's a market for it.

114
00:16:21.624 --> 00:16:23.918
I mean. what if there's a plague?

115
00:16:24.001 --> 00:16:26.670
What have you had. Betty.
like. one beer?

116
00:16:26.754 --> 00:16:29.715
I'm just sa...
I'm just saying. you know.

117
00:16:29.757 --> 00:16:32.218
frogs start falling from the sky.

118
00:16:32.259 --> 00:16:34.595
who do they come to?

119
00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.639
We'd be world-renowned.

120
00:16:36.681 --> 00:16:38.891
Make any parents proud.

121
00:16:40.101 --> 00:16:42.019
I bet they would be.

122
00:16:42.103 --> 00:16:45.064
They actually did
want me to be a scientist.

123
00:16:46.232 --> 00:16:48.234
I mean. your birth parents.

124
00:16:49.985 --> 00:16:51.946
Guess we'll never know.

125
00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.952
I don't understand why you don't
want to find out about them.

126
00:16:57.993 --> 00:17:01.455
They're dead.  They died before
I can remember anything.

127
00:17:01.455 --> 00:17:04.375
Why do you always
come back to this?

128
00:17:04.458 --> 00:17:06.711
Don't know.

129
00:17:06.794 --> 00:17:10.131
I guess I figure there's more
to you than you like to show.

130
00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.259
I guess there couldn't be any less

131
00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:17.471
Right. So now we come
full circle back to that.

132
00:17:17.513 --> 00:17:19.515
Nice work. Betty.

133
00:17:32.862 --> 00:17:34.864
Betty.

134
00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.616
- Glen.
- Hey.

135
00:17:37.658 --> 00:17:39.660
Hi.

136
00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.787
Hi.

137
00:17:43.164 --> 00:17:45.374
What happened
to your uniform?

138
00:17:45.374 --> 00:17:47.626
Oh. I. uh...
I switched over.

139
00:17:47.668 --> 00:17:50.129
I'm still working with your father. but...

140
00:17:50.171 --> 00:17:53.799
Well. you know. the military's subcontracting
out all the most interesting work. and...

141
00:17:55.342 --> 00:17:57.345
Can't argue with a paycheck.

142
00:17:57.428 --> 00:18:00.348
I basically run
all the labs on the base now.

143
00:18:00.431 --> 00:18:02.350
Oh.

144
00:18:03.976 --> 00:18:06.145
Hey. you're uh...

145
00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.230
you're looking good.

146
00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.489
You're the genetics expert.

147
00:18:27.917 --> 00:18:30.628
Ah. the good old college days.

148
00:18:32.046 --> 00:18:34.048
So. how's business?

149
00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.010
What do you want?

150
00:18:39.637 --> 00:18:42.556
All right. I'll cut to the chase.

151
00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.559
I've been hearing interesting things
about what you guys are doing here

152
00:18:45.643 --> 00:18:49.522
Your little molecular machines
have some incredible implications.

153
00:18:49.647 --> 00:18:52.566
How would you like to
come work for Atheon?

154
00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.569
Get paid 10 times as much
as you earn now...

155
00:18:55.653 --> 00:18:58.364
and own a piece of the patents.

156
00:19:00.199 --> 00:19:02.159
You just have to say the word.

157
00:19:02.243 --> 00:19:04.245
Two words: The door.

158
00:19:23.514 --> 00:19:25.433
General?

159
00:19:25.516 --> 00:19:27.643
Come in.

160
00:19:28.728 --> 00:19:31.355
Talbot wanted you to see this. sir.

161
00:19:31.439 --> 00:19:35.401
It's about a lab Atheon is targeting for
acquisition and removal to desert base

162
00:19:36.652 --> 00:19:38.821
Why isn't it
going through N.S.C.?

163
00:19:40.656 --> 00:19:44.243
It. uh. concerns
your daughter. sir.

164
00:19:52.043 --> 00:19:54.503
Hi. Sorry.

165
00:19:56.172 --> 00:20:00.384
Hey. what happened to Benny?  Is he
not working the night shift anymore?

166
00:20:00.468 --> 00:20:02.428
Benny's dead.

167
00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.764
I'm the new guy.

168
00:20:04.847 --> 00:20:06.849
Oh.

169
00:20:08.351 --> 00:20:10.478
Good to meet you.
Same.

170
00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.921
- Let's try another.

171
00:20:37.004 --> 00:20:39.799
Mmm. no. Stay here.

172
00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.967
I look tired anyway.

173
00:20:42.051 --> 00:20:44.220
Yeah. but you look great.

174
00:20:46.889 --> 00:20:48.849
What's the matter?

175
00:20:48.891 --> 00:20:51.435
It's these dreams. Doctor.

176
00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:54.814
I keep having them.
and they're terrible.

177
00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.567
Tell me about your dream.

178
00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.656
Well. it starts...

179
00:21:03.781 --> 00:21:07.034
it starts with a memory...
I think it's my first memory.

180
00:21:07.118 --> 00:21:10.121
It's this image I have...

181
00:21:10.204 --> 00:21:12.998
from when I was
maybe two years old.

182
00:21:44.739 --> 00:21:47.158
Do you think
it's just a dream?

183
00:21:47.241 --> 00:21:49.493
No. I think it's something
that happened...

184
00:21:49.577 --> 00:21:52.580
when I was living at a desert base
with my father.

185
00:21:53.581 --> 00:21:55.583
Anyhow.

186
00:21:55.666 --> 00:21:58.127
the dream goes on and...

187
00:21:58.169 --> 00:22:00.046
suddenly I'm alone.

188
00:22:35.498 --> 00:22:37.458
That's terrible.

189
00:22:37.541 --> 00:22:39.960
You know I'd never hurt you.

190
00:23:15.496 --> 00:23:17.498
Hey there.

191
00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.626
What's your name. darlin'?

192
00:23:21.627 --> 00:23:23.504
Eh? What's your name?

193
00:23:24.255 --> 00:23:26.716
Okay.

194
00:23:26.799 --> 00:23:28.801
It's okay.

195
00:25:19.328 --> 00:25:21.288
I gotta talk to you. Edith.

196
00:25:21.372 --> 00:25:23.457
Bruce. stay here!

197
00:26:43.704 --> 00:26:46.707
"C... T... G...

198
00:26:46.791 --> 00:26:50.002
A... G."

199
00:26:52.213 --> 00:26:54.173
Bruce.

200
00:27:00.388 --> 00:27:02.306
My Bruce.

201
00:27:11.774 --> 00:27:14.235
Good morning.
Glen dropped by.

202
00:27:14.276 --> 00:27:16.237
What's he doing here?

203
00:27:16.278 --> 00:27:17.988
You know. Dr. Krenzler.

204
00:27:18.072 --> 00:27:21.033
you and I have never had the chance
to get to know each other properly.

205
00:27:21.117 --> 00:27:25.121
Well. that's because I don't want to get
to know you. properly or improperly.

206
00:27:27.248 --> 00:27:29.166
So leave.

207
00:27:29.250 --> 00:27:31.210
Hey. no worries.

208
00:27:39.427 --> 00:27:41.762
Let me give you a little heads-up.

209
00:27:42.805 --> 00:27:45.266
There is a hairsbreadth
between friendly offer...

210
00:27:45.349 --> 00:27:47.226
and hostile takeover.

211
00:27:47.351 --> 00:27:51.272
I've done my homework.  The work
you're doing here is dynamite.

212
00:27:51.355 --> 00:27:54.275
Think: Gls embedded with technology...

213
00:27:54.316 --> 00:27:56.819
that makes them instantly
repairable on the battlefield...

214
00:27:56.902 --> 00:27:59.030
in our sole possession.

215
00:28:00.114 --> 00:28:02.575
That's a hell of a business.

216
00:28:02.616 --> 00:28:06.495
Well. it's not what we're doing here.
We're doing the basic science for everyone

217
00:28:08.748 --> 00:28:11.083
You know. someday
I'm gonna write a book...

218
00:28:11.125 --> 00:28:16.130
and I'm gonna call it When Stupid Ideals
Happen To Smart. Penniless Scientists.

219
00:28:17.131 --> 00:28:20.259
In the meantime. Bruce.
you will be hearing from me.

220
00:28:42.782 --> 00:28:44.784
About Glen. I. um...

221
00:28:44.867 --> 00:28:47.536
There's nothing to talk about.

222
00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:51.832
Okay.

223
00:28:51.874 --> 00:28:55.878
I just wanted to say. don't worry
about him... I'll handle it.

224
00:28:58.339 --> 00:29:00.299
How?

225
00:29:01.384 --> 00:29:03.427
I'm gonna call my father.

226
00:29:04.637 --> 00:29:06.555
ask him to exert some pressure.

227
00:29:06.639 --> 00:29:09.975
Last I heard. you and your father
weren't speaking.

228
00:29:09.975 --> 00:29:11.977
Hmm.

229
00:29:12.019 --> 00:29:13.979
Well...

230
00:29:14.021 --> 00:29:16.691
I guess now I have something
to talk with him about.

231
00:29:17.191 --> 00:29:19.110
I think this circuit's kinda fried.

232
00:29:19.193 --> 00:29:22.071
I don't know.  Maybe you
anna come take a look at it

233
00:29:22.113 --> 00:29:24.448
Okay. I'll be right there.

234
00:29:31.747 --> 00:29:33.999
Aah!

235
00:29:50.433 --> 00:29:54.353
The gamma's too high!
Bruce. I can't stop it!

236
00:29:56.397 --> 00:29:59.066
Harper. get out!

237
00:29:59.066 --> 00:30:01.819
Get out!

238
00:30:27.595 --> 00:30:29.513
How's Harper?

239
00:30:29.638 --> 00:30:31.515
He's all right.

240
00:30:31.599 --> 00:30:33.517
You saved him.

241
00:30:33.601 --> 00:30:37.563
I don't think he's coming back
to the lab for a while. though.

242
00:30:42.818 --> 00:30:45.363
I don't understand
how this is possible.

243
00:30:46.530 --> 00:30:48.324
You should be dead.

244
00:30:50.451 --> 00:30:54.038
They worked... the nanomeds.

245
00:30:54.121 --> 00:30:56.123
I mean. I feel great.

246
00:30:56.165 --> 00:30:59.710
I feel like... I don't know.
They must have. like. fixed me.

247
00:30:59.752 --> 00:31:03.297
Bruce. they've killed everything else
that they've come into contact with.

248
00:31:05.675 --> 00:31:07.635
Are you sure
the doctor checked?

249
00:31:07.677 --> 00:31:09.637
The doctor gave me
the full workup.

250
00:31:09.637 --> 00:31:11.931
He wants to know where
he can get what I'm taking.

251
00:31:12.014 --> 00:31:13.974
I'm a hundred percent.

252
00:31:15.017 --> 00:31:17.019
More.

253
00:31:17.103 --> 00:31:19.397
What do you mean?

254
00:31:19.480 --> 00:31:21.399
Remember my bad knee?

255
00:31:21.482 --> 00:31:23.818
Well. now it's my good knee.

256
00:31:23.859 --> 00:31:26.404
Bruce. this isn't funny.

257
00:31:26.487 --> 00:31:28.489
I was watching you.

258
00:31:29.657 --> 00:31:34.036
You were gonna die.
and I was gonna have to watch you die.

259
00:31:34.120 --> 00:31:36.747
Betty...

260
00:31:36.831 --> 00:31:38.874
I'm sorry.

261
00:31:40.543 --> 00:31:43.129
Really.

262
00:31:43.212 --> 00:31:45.798
Hey. I'm not gonna explode.
Okay?

263
00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:48.801
Yeah.

264
00:31:48.843 --> 00:31:51.971
You should get some rest.

265
00:31:52.054 --> 00:31:54.056
And I'm fine. Really.

266
00:31:55.391 --> 00:31:57.393
I've never felt better.

267
00:33:00.122 --> 00:33:02.958
Your name is not Krenzler.

268
00:33:03.125 --> 00:33:05.336
It's Banner.

269
00:33:08.631 --> 00:33:10.675
- What?
- Your name...

270
00:33:10.675 --> 00:33:12.468
it's Banner.

271
00:33:12.760 --> 00:33:14.220
Bruce Banner.

272
00:33:14.970 --> 00:33:17.181
Bruce.

273
00:33:18.766 --> 00:33:21.435
How did you get in here?
I work here now.

274
00:33:21.519 --> 00:33:24.271
In the labs.
The late shift.

275
00:33:25.439 --> 00:33:28.275
It keeps me close to you.

276
00:33:28.359 --> 00:33:32.697
You always work so late yourself
with your friend Miss Ross.

277
00:33:32.780 --> 00:33:36.075
No. no. Please. Please.
Let me.

278
00:33:39.662 --> 00:33:41.789
You're not well.

279
00:33:41.956 --> 00:33:44.625
You've had a terrible accident.

280
00:33:46.794 --> 00:33:49.755
You're wondering
why you're still alive.

281
00:33:51.966 --> 00:33:54.969
You're thinking
there's something inside.

282
00:33:55.970 --> 00:33:58.431
Something different...

283
00:34:00.307 --> 00:34:02.184
inexplicable.

284
00:34:03.728 --> 00:34:06.647
I can help you understand.

285
00:34:06.731 --> 00:34:08.733
if you'll let me.

286
00:34:10.401 --> 00:34:12.403
If you'll...

287
00:34:13.487 --> 00:34:15.448
forgive me.

288
00:34:19.326 --> 00:34:24.165
Look. mister. I'm sure I have
nothing to forgive you for.

289
00:34:25.624 --> 00:34:27.585
So perhaps you should leave now.

290
00:34:27.668 --> 00:34:29.587
I'll be fine.

291
00:34:29.670 --> 00:34:31.589
You must know.

292
00:34:31.672 --> 00:34:33.924
You may not want to believe it.

293
00:34:34.008 --> 00:34:37.636
but I can see it in your eyes.

294
00:34:38.846 --> 00:34:41.349
So much like your mother's.

295
00:34:42.475 --> 00:34:45.186
Of course.
you're my flesh and blood.

296
00:34:45.269 --> 00:34:49.357
But then. you're something else too.
aren't you?

297
00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:51.692
My physical son.

298
00:34:52.693 --> 00:34:55.363
but the child of my mind too.

299
00:34:55.446 --> 00:34:57.365
No.

300
00:34:57.448 --> 00:34:59.325
You're lying.

301
00:34:59.450 --> 00:35:02.328
My parents died
when I was a small boy.

302
00:35:02.370 --> 00:35:05.873
No. no. that's not true.
That's what they wanted you to believe.

303
00:35:05.915 --> 00:35:09.168
The experiments. the accident...
all top secret.

304
00:35:09.210 --> 00:35:12.296
They put me away for 30 years.

305
00:35:12.380 --> 00:35:14.799
Thirty years!

306
00:35:15.841 --> 00:35:18.010
Away from you.

307
00:35:18.094 --> 00:35:20.054
Away from our work.

308
00:35:21.263 --> 00:35:23.224
But they couldn't keep me forever.

309
00:35:23.224 --> 00:35:26.018
After all. I'm sane.
They had to admit it.

310
00:35:27.603 --> 00:35:30.272
You see.

311
00:35:30.356 --> 00:35:32.316
everything...

312
00:35:32.400 --> 00:35:34.694
your extraordinary mind...

313
00:35:34.735 --> 00:35:37.738
has been seeking all these years...

314
00:35:37.822 --> 00:35:40.324
it's been inside you.

315
00:35:41.325 --> 00:35:43.577
Now we will understand it.

316
00:35:43.661 --> 00:35:46.080
We will harness it.

317
00:35:48.165 --> 00:35:50.418
No. don't answer it.
It's Miss Ross again.

318
00:35:50.501 --> 00:35:54.922
There's something you need to know
about her. Bruce. Something troublesome

319
00:35:54.964 --> 00:35:57.591
Let me protect you from her.

320
00:35:57.675 --> 00:36:00.219
No. Get out.

321
00:36:00.302 --> 00:36:02.680
- Bruce...
- Get out!

322
00:36:03.389 --> 00:36:04.682
Sit!

323
00:36:22.199 --> 00:36:25.411
We're gonna have to
watch that temper of yours.

324
00:37:04.950 --> 00:37:06.827
You sure you're okay?

325
00:37:06.952 --> 00:37:08.871
Yeah. just glad to be out of bed

326
00:37:10.122 --> 00:37:12.708
Got a message from my father.

327
00:37:12.792 --> 00:37:14.710
He's coming to see me.

328
00:37:14.794 --> 00:37:16.712
Your father?

329
00:37:16.796 --> 00:37:18.464
When?

330
00:37:18.464 --> 00:37:20.508
Lands in about an hour.

331
00:37:21.509 --> 00:37:24.470
The funny thing is. he called me.

332
00:37:35.314 --> 00:37:38.442
- Hi. Dad.
- Hello. Betty.

333
00:37:48.244 --> 00:37:50.121
- Here. ma'am.
- Thanks.

334
00:37:50.204 --> 00:37:51.622
- You're welcome.  Sir?
- Thank you.

335
00:37:51.706 --> 00:37:53.082
You're welcome.

336
00:38:01.590 --> 00:38:05.219
Look. I'm gonna get right to it.

337
00:38:05.302 --> 00:38:07.388
It's about Glen. isn't it?

338
00:38:08.848 --> 00:38:11.809
He's been snooping around my lab.

339
00:38:11.892 --> 00:38:13.811
Glen noticed some things.

340
00:38:13.894 --> 00:38:16.731
asked me to make some inquiries.

341
00:38:18.482 --> 00:38:20.317
Are you here to...

342
00:38:20.484 --> 00:38:22.403
question me?

343
00:38:22.528 --> 00:38:23.988
No.

344
00:38:24.030 --> 00:38:26.866
We've turned up
some surprising things.

345
00:38:29.368 --> 00:38:31.704
This Krenzler you work with...

346
00:38:31.787 --> 00:38:34.331
you know who he really is?

347
00:38:36.292 --> 00:38:38.419
How much do you
actually know about him?

348
00:38:38.461 --> 00:38:41.422
I think the question is.

349
00:38:41.422 --> 00:38:44.258
what is it
that you know about him?

350
00:38:46.552 --> 00:38:51.515
- Well. right now. I'm not...
- Not at liberty to disclose it to me. Right

351
00:38:52.767 --> 00:38:54.727
You know.

352
00:38:54.769 --> 00:38:57.813
I think I was hoping that...

353
00:38:57.813 --> 00:39:00.566
maybe this time you just...

354
00:39:00.608 --> 00:39:04.028
honestly wanted to see me again.

355
00:39:04.070 --> 00:39:06.697
- You've got this all wrong. Betty.
- Do I?

356
00:39:06.781 --> 00:39:10.701
Yes. I do want to see you.

357
00:39:13.037 --> 00:39:16.165
I really wishthat I
could believe you.

358
00:40:03.671 --> 00:40:05.715
Everything...

359
00:40:05.840 --> 00:40:09.260
your extraordinary mind
has been seeking...

360
00:40:09.343 --> 00:40:11.679
all these years.

361
00:40:11.762 --> 00:40:14.432
it's been inside you.

362
00:40:33.117 --> 00:40:35.286
Hi. you've called Dr. Krenzler.

363
00:40:35.369 --> 00:40:38.372
Please leave a message
and I'll call you right back.

364
00:40:39.749 --> 00:40:43.377
Bruce. hey. Are you there?

365
00:40:43.461 --> 00:40:45.880
Look. um.
I think I screwed up.

366
00:40:45.921 --> 00:40:50.551
My father... It's like he suspects
you of something. I don't know.

367
00:40:50.634 --> 00:40:53.721
- I was so impatient. like always.

368
00:40:53.804 --> 00:40:56.682
I didn't hear him out.
I don't know. I...

369
00:40:56.724 --> 00:41:00.186
I just think that they're planning
something with the lab.

370
00:41:00.269 --> 00:41:01.979
So. um. uh...

371
00:41:02.063 --> 00:41:03.898
Call me. Okay?

372
00:41:03.981 --> 00:41:05.816
Bye.

373
00:41:07.818 --> 00:41:08.986
- Betty?

374
00:42:46.125 --> 00:42:49.045
Dispatch! Dispatch!
We have a 415 at the lab!

375
00:42:49.128 --> 00:42:51.464
Send Berkeley P.D. Now!
Send 'em now!

376
00:43:18.824 --> 00:43:20.785
Watch out!

377
00:44:25.725 --> 00:44:28.060
Edith?

378
00:44:28.102 --> 00:44:30.062
David. what's going on?

379
00:44:30.104 --> 00:44:33.315
- I gotta talk to you. Edith.
- Bruce. stay here.

380
00:45:05.514 --> 00:45:07.683
My Bruce.

381
00:45:21.822 --> 00:45:23.824
Bruce?

382
00:46:00.152 --> 00:46:02.655
There was some sort of explosion.

383
00:46:02.738 --> 00:46:05.199
They wouldn't let us
into the building.

384
00:46:06.575 --> 00:46:09.036
I was worried about you.

385
00:46:09.120 --> 00:46:11.580
Well. I'm okay.

386
00:46:13.499 --> 00:46:15.459
What happened to you last night?

387
00:46:17.086 --> 00:46:19.505
I had the most vivid dream.

388
00:46:20.798 --> 00:46:23.718
It was like being born.

389
00:46:23.801 --> 00:46:26.512
Coming up for air.
Light hitting my face.

390
00:46:26.595 --> 00:46:28.597
Screaming.

391
00:46:29.598 --> 00:46:32.018
My heartbeat...

392
00:46:32.143 --> 00:46:34.645
it was. like. boom...

393
00:46:34.729 --> 00:46:36.689
boom...

394
00:46:39.483 --> 00:46:41.485
boom.

395
00:46:46.699 --> 00:46:48.659
Were you at the lab?

396
00:46:48.701 --> 00:46:50.703
No.

397
00:46:52.038 --> 00:46:54.040
But something...

398
00:46:56.459 --> 00:46:58.377
And there was that man.

399
00:46:58.461 --> 00:47:00.379
The one with the dogs.

400
00:47:00.463 --> 00:47:02.423
Who?

401
00:47:03.883 --> 00:47:06.552
That new janitor.

402
00:47:06.594 --> 00:47:08.929
He said he was my father.

403
00:47:14.060 --> 00:47:16.228
I'll get it.

404
00:47:26.447 --> 00:47:28.449
My father.

405
00:47:38.042 --> 00:47:40.127
My. my.

406
00:47:40.169 --> 00:47:42.421
So this is the young Bruce Ban...

407
00:47:44.674 --> 00:47:47.093
Krenzler.

408
00:47:48.678 --> 00:47:52.598
I think you left something
in your lab last night.

409
00:47:54.684 --> 00:47:56.435
Mitchell.

410
00:47:56.477 --> 00:47:59.313
Escort my daughter outside.
I'll join her shortly.

411
00:48:01.023 --> 00:48:02.817
I'd rather stay here.

412
00:48:02.900 --> 00:48:05.403
Now. Betty.

413
00:48:06.737 --> 00:48:08.698
It's okay.

414
00:48:08.739 --> 00:48:10.700
I'll be fine.

415
00:48:21.752 --> 00:48:24.255
Keep him under observation.
I'll be back.

416
00:48:31.679 --> 00:48:34.724
- What?
- Your friend in there.

417
00:48:34.765 --> 00:48:38.477
There's a good chance he's caught
up in some very bad business.

418
00:48:38.561 --> 00:48:40.479
Unfinished business.

419
00:48:40.563 --> 00:48:43.649
And I promise you. I'm gonna
get to the bottom of it.

420
00:48:43.774 --> 00:48:46.652
You have my word
I'll make sure he's cared for.

421
00:48:46.736 --> 00:48:49.655
But as of right now.
he is incommunicado.

422
00:48:49.739 --> 00:48:52.158
And for the next
few days at least.

423
00:48:52.241 --> 00:48:54.118
you're gonna stay away from here.

424
00:48:54.201 --> 00:48:56.203
For your own good.

425
00:49:04.628 --> 00:49:08.299
Okay. and that's for the new guy
on the night shift. right?

426
00:49:08.341 --> 00:49:11.344
Great. Thank you.
I appreciate it.

427
00:49:28.736 --> 00:49:30.738
Dr. Ross.

428
00:49:30.780 --> 00:49:33.741
How unexpected.

429
00:49:33.824 --> 00:49:35.826
Please come in.

430
00:49:41.165 --> 00:49:44.752
I'm sorry to just show up
at your house like this.

431
00:49:44.835 --> 00:49:46.879
Uh...

432
00:49:49.799 --> 00:49:52.301
I came to ask you something that...

433
00:49:52.385 --> 00:49:56.097
I really have no business asking

434
00:49:57.682 --> 00:50:00.101
He told you?

435
00:50:00.184 --> 00:50:02.186
He said you talked to him.

436
00:50:02.269 --> 00:50:04.230
Oh.

437
00:50:04.271 --> 00:50:06.273
Please sit down.

438
00:50:14.699 --> 00:50:18.494
Bruce was at the lab last night.
He said that you were there too.

439
00:50:18.577 --> 00:50:21.455
But he can't remember much about it

440
00:50:21.539 --> 00:50:23.708
I need to find out what happened.

441
00:50:23.791 --> 00:50:25.793
So. you want to know. uh.

442
00:50:25.793 --> 00:50:27.878
what's wrong with him...

443
00:50:28.796 --> 00:50:30.923
so you can fix him?

444
00:50:31.048 --> 00:50:33.384
Cure him. change him.

445
00:50:35.386 --> 00:50:37.805
My father's with the military.

446
00:50:37.888 --> 00:50:40.808
He seems to think he's involved in
some kind of threat to national security

447
00:50:40.891 --> 00:50:42.810
Mmm.

448
00:50:42.893 --> 00:50:46.272
Your father. Ross.

449
00:50:47.314 --> 00:50:51.110
You brought your father
down upon his head?

450
00:50:51.193 --> 00:50:54.196
How little you understand.
Miss Ross.

451
00:50:54.238 --> 00:50:58.117
and how dangerous
your ignorance has become.

452
00:50:59.827 --> 00:51:02.079
I'm sorry.
Don't be sorry.

453
00:51:02.163 --> 00:51:04.206
My son is...

454
00:51:05.666 --> 00:51:07.626
unique.

455
00:51:07.668 --> 00:51:09.587
That's why you can't relate to him.

456
00:51:09.670 --> 00:51:14.300
And because he is unique. the world
will not tolerate his existence.

457
00:51:14.342 --> 00:51:16.302
Will they?

458
00:51:17.428 --> 00:51:19.430
But you...

459
00:51:21.057 --> 00:51:22.808
you try.

460
00:51:22.850 --> 00:51:24.810
don't you?

461
00:51:24.852 --> 00:51:26.896
Yes.

462
00:51:32.109 --> 00:51:35.613
And a very beautiful
woman like you.

463
00:51:35.696 --> 00:51:38.449
your attentions...

464
00:51:38.532 --> 00:51:42.203
can't be completely unwanted.

465
00:51:43.162 --> 00:51:44.705
Can they?

466
00:51:46.040 --> 00:51:48.292
No.

467
00:51:48.334 --> 00:51:51.837
Not with eyes like yours.

468
00:51:51.879 --> 00:51:54.799
watching expectantly.

469
00:51:55.841 --> 00:51:57.927
lovingly.

470
00:52:00.513 --> 00:52:03.349
But I'm afraid
we're both too late to help him.

471
00:52:03.432 --> 00:52:05.643
There's nothing
I can do for him...

472
00:52:05.726 --> 00:52:07.853
or for you.

473
00:52:07.937 --> 00:52:09.939
Besides.

474
00:52:11.232 --> 00:52:13.859
he's made it clear he wants
nothing to do with me.

475
00:52:13.984 --> 00:52:15.861
His choice.

476
00:52:15.986 --> 00:52:19.782
Now. if you'll excuse me. Miss Ross.
I have some work to do.

477
00:52:19.865 --> 00:52:23.077
And don't worry about the dogs.

478
00:52:23.202 --> 00:52:25.079
You'll be fine.

479
00:52:25.204 --> 00:52:27.707
Just don't look 'em in the eyes.

480
00:52:30.251 --> 00:52:32.128
Good-bye.

481
00:52:34.171 --> 00:52:37.633
He gets released. and a month later
your lab is destroyed.

482
00:52:37.717 --> 00:52:39.593
What a coincidence.

483
00:52:39.719 --> 00:52:42.638
So you're not gonna tell me
where he is. are ya?

484
00:52:42.722 --> 00:52:45.933
How many times do I have to tell you?
I'd like to help you. but I just don't know

485
00:52:46.058 --> 00:52:48.310
You know who I am.
Right. Banner?

486
00:52:48.394 --> 00:52:51.188
- Your Betty's father.
You're a high-ranking general.
- Let's cut the crap.

487
00:52:51.313 --> 00:52:55.067
I'm the guy who had your father
tossed away. and a lot more like him.

488
00:52:55.109 --> 00:52:58.779
and I'll do the same with you if I
feel so disposed. You understand?

489
00:52:58.904 --> 00:53:01.282
If you had him tossed away.
then why are you asking me?

490
00:53:01.323 --> 00:53:05.411
I don't remember.
I was always told my father was dead.

491
00:53:05.494 --> 00:53:07.413
Don't play with me!

492
00:53:07.496 --> 00:53:09.915
You were four years old
when you saw it.

493
00:53:10.041 --> 00:53:12.460
When I saw what?

494
00:53:12.501 --> 00:53:16.339
You were right there.  How could
anyone forget a thing like that?

495
00:53:17.548 --> 00:53:19.467
What?

496
00:53:19.550 --> 00:53:22.553
Oh. some more repressed memories.

497
00:53:25.639 --> 00:53:27.641
Just tell me.

498
00:53:30.394 --> 00:53:32.897
I'm sorry. son.

499
00:53:33.898 --> 00:53:37.443
You're an even more screwed-up mess
than I thought you'd be.

500
00:53:38.444 --> 00:53:40.946
Until we get
to the bottom of this.

501
00:53:40.988 --> 00:53:43.991
your lab has been declared
a top-secret military site...

502
00:53:44.033 --> 00:53:47.453
and you're not gonna get
a security clearance to get back into it...

503
00:53:47.536 --> 00:53:50.498
or any other lab that's doing
anything more interesting than...

504
00:53:50.539 --> 00:53:54.085
trying to figure out
the next generation of herbal hair gel.

505
00:53:57.672 --> 00:53:59.715
One more thing.

506
00:53:59.799 --> 00:54:01.759
If you ever...

507
00:54:01.884 --> 00:54:06.472
come within a thousand yards
of my daughter again.

508
00:54:06.514 --> 00:54:09.725
I'll put you away for the
rest of your natural life.

509
00:54:24.031 --> 00:54:25.950
Dogs!

510
00:54:28.035 --> 00:54:30.955
Go! Go get her!

511
00:54:31.038 --> 00:54:34.041
And let nothing stand in your way!

512
00:54:34.083 --> 00:54:36.377
Go!

513
00:55:40.524 --> 00:55:42.443
Hello?

514
00:55:42.568 --> 00:55:44.445
Bruce?

515
00:55:44.528 --> 00:55:48.532
So. they think they can just
throw you away as they did me.

516
00:55:56.832 --> 00:55:59.502
What's wrong with me?
What did you do to me?

517
00:55:59.585 --> 00:56:01.504
I got a visit today.

518
00:56:01.587 --> 00:56:03.964
A very unwelcome visit.

519
00:56:04.006 --> 00:56:06.592
I'm afraid my hand is being forced

520
00:56:06.676 --> 00:56:09.845
What did you do to me?

521
00:56:09.929 --> 00:56:12.848
You so much want to know. don't you?

522
00:56:12.932 --> 00:56:17.103
But I think no explanation
will serve you half as well...

523
00:56:17.144 --> 00:56:19.689
as the experience.

524
00:56:19.814 --> 00:56:24.568
In any case. I still don't
quite understand it myself.

525
00:56:24.610 --> 00:56:27.613
If they'd only let me
work in peace...

526
00:56:27.613 --> 00:56:30.783
Of course. my betters
would have none of that.

527
00:56:30.866 --> 00:56:33.786
So you experimented
on yourself. didn't you?

528
00:56:33.869 --> 00:56:37.540
And passed on to me... what?

529
00:56:37.623 --> 00:56:40.167
An alteration. Genetic.

530
00:56:40.292 --> 00:56:44.547
A deformity.
I guess you could call it that.

531
00:56:44.630 --> 00:56:47.174
But an amazing strength too.

532
00:56:47.258 --> 00:56:50.219
And now. finally unleashed.
I can harvest it.

533
00:56:50.302 --> 00:56:52.179
No.

534
00:56:52.263 --> 00:56:54.181
You'll do no such thing.

535
00:56:54.265 --> 00:56:56.767
I will isolate it
and treat it myself.

536
00:56:56.809 --> 00:57:00.229
I'll remove it and I'll kill it
before it does any real harm.

537
00:57:00.271 --> 00:57:03.149
I'll bet you and your Betty
would love to destroy it.

538
00:57:03.232 --> 00:57:06.444
But would you really
destroy part of yourself?

539
00:57:07.486 --> 00:57:10.114
I don't think so.

540
00:57:10.197 --> 00:57:12.116
And as for Betty.

541
00:57:12.199 --> 00:57:14.201
I'm sending her a surprise visit...

542
00:57:14.243 --> 00:57:16.662
from some four-legged
friends of mine.

543
00:57:16.746 --> 00:57:21.250
You see. I managed to culture
some of your very own DNA. Bruce.

544
00:57:21.334 --> 00:57:24.003
and the results are tremendous.

545
00:57:24.045 --> 00:57:27.840
They're unstable. but very powerful.

546
00:57:29.300 --> 00:57:31.469
What about my DNA?

547
00:57:31.552 --> 00:57:35.598
Let's just wait and see what Betty
makes of the results. huh?

548
00:57:35.681 --> 00:57:37.600
No. You're crazy.

549
00:57:37.683 --> 00:57:39.643
I won't let you.

550
00:57:42.688 --> 00:57:45.399
Get your hands off of me.
Talbot. what's this...

551
00:57:45.483 --> 00:57:47.777
Inside. asshole.
I wanna talk to you.

552
00:57:47.860 --> 00:57:49.779
Listen. my father's
going after Betty...

553
00:57:49.862 --> 00:57:53.115
What makes you think you can go behind
my back and get Ross to cut me out. huh?

554
00:57:53.199 --> 00:57:56.577
Listen to me!
Betty's in trouble!

555
00:57:59.914 --> 00:58:01.916
You pathetic freak.

556
00:58:01.957 --> 00:58:04.377
Betty's in danger.
I swear to you. she'll be killed.

557
00:58:04.418 --> 00:58:06.337
I can state the obvious.

558
00:58:06.420 --> 00:58:09.715
Something tells me you aren't in much of a
position to be making stupid threats to anyone

559
00:58:14.679 --> 00:58:16.764
- Talbot.
- Yeah?

560
00:58:16.847 --> 00:58:18.724
You're making me angry.

561
00:58:18.808 --> 00:58:21.102
Oh. am I?

562
00:59:14.530 --> 00:59:16.782
Ohh! Oh!

563
00:59:16.824 --> 00:59:19.160
I got him! Open fire!

564
01:01:09.311 --> 01:01:12.064
Bruce?

565
01:06:38.808 --> 01:06:42.103
He sent these dogs. didn't he?

566
01:06:42.228 --> 01:06:44.605
But I killed them!

567
01:07:09.505 --> 01:07:11.549
My God.

568
01:07:11.632 --> 01:07:14.301
It must be the nanomeds.
It must be the gamma exposure.

569
01:07:14.385 --> 01:07:17.138
But we've never seen
any effect like this before.

570
01:07:17.221 --> 01:07:19.140
No. Deeper.

571
01:07:19.223 --> 01:07:22.768
The gamma just unleashed
what was already there.

572
01:07:22.852 --> 01:07:25.396
Unleashed what?

573
01:07:25.479 --> 01:07:28.482
Me.

574
01:07:28.566 --> 01:07:31.277
It.

575
01:07:31.360 --> 01:07:33.904
It's okay.

576
01:07:33.988 --> 01:07:35.656
Shh. It's okay.

577
01:07:37.450 --> 01:07:40.119
What were those animals?

578
01:07:40.202 --> 01:07:43.164
My father sent them.

579
01:07:43.289 --> 01:07:46.000
He is my father.

580
01:07:46.083 --> 01:07:48.169
He wanted me to change.

581
01:07:48.252 --> 01:07:51.589
He wanted me to change
into that mindless hulk.

582
01:07:51.672 --> 01:07:53.799
Why would he want that?

583
01:07:55.217 --> 01:07:57.470
Can you remember anything?

584
01:07:57.511 --> 01:08:00.806
Is there anything
from when you were changed?

585
01:08:03.601 --> 01:08:06.520
It was like a dream.

586
01:08:06.604 --> 01:08:09.482
About what?

587
01:08:10.858 --> 01:08:12.860
Rage.

588
01:08:14.320 --> 01:08:16.322
Power.

589
01:08:17.907 --> 01:08:20.368
And freedom.

590
01:08:38.219 --> 01:08:41.555
Hello? Sir.

591
01:08:42.973 --> 01:08:44.975
- Hello.
- Dad?

592
01:08:45.017 --> 01:08:47.395
Betty! Are you all right?

593
01:08:49.605 --> 01:08:53.234
I'm scared.
I need your help.

594
01:08:53.317 --> 01:08:55.319
Where are you?

595
01:09:05.746 --> 01:09:08.082
How are you?

596
01:09:08.165 --> 01:09:10.793
Okay. I guess.

597
01:09:14.463 --> 01:09:16.799
I think that somehow...

598
01:09:16.882 --> 01:09:20.177
your anger is triggering
the nanomeds.

599
01:09:20.177 --> 01:09:24.640
How could it?  We designed them
to respond to physical damage.

600
01:09:24.724 --> 01:09:27.810
Emotional damage
can manifest physically.

601
01:09:29.228 --> 01:09:31.397
Like what?

602
01:09:34.525 --> 01:09:36.652
Serious trauma.

603
01:09:38.529 --> 01:09:40.573
Repressed memories.

604
01:09:46.037 --> 01:09:50.875
Your father grilled me about something that
happened to me from early childhood...

605
01:09:50.958 --> 01:09:53.252
that I'm supposed to remember.

606
01:09:53.377 --> 01:09:54.795
He did?

607
01:09:54.837 --> 01:09:59.884
It sounded bad.
but... I honestly don't remember.

608
01:10:03.054 --> 01:10:05.598
The thing that worries me...

609
01:10:05.681 --> 01:10:07.683
is...

610
01:10:07.767 --> 01:10:09.852
a physical wound is finite.

611
01:10:09.935 --> 01:10:11.854
but with emotions.

612
01:10:11.937 --> 01:10:15.733
what's to say it won't
just go on and on...

613
01:10:15.775 --> 01:10:19.320
and start a chain reaction?

614
01:10:21.489 --> 01:10:24.116
You know what scares me the most?

615
01:10:26.035 --> 01:10:28.079
When it happens.

616
01:10:29.246 --> 01:10:31.374
when it comes over me...

617
01:10:31.457 --> 01:10:34.502
and I totally lose control.

618
01:10:36.295 --> 01:10:38.339
I like it.

619
01:10:55.481 --> 01:10:58.150
It's okay. I got you.
I'm sorry.

620
01:10:58.317 --> 01:11:01.987
You'll be okay.
It's just to make you sleep.

621
01:11:02.029 --> 01:11:03.906
Target down.
Target secure.

622
01:11:04.031 --> 01:11:06.826
I'm going to take you someplace safe

623
01:11:06.867 --> 01:11:10.121
Okay? Bruce?

624
01:11:10.162 --> 01:11:12.665
Bruce?

625
01:11:12.707 --> 01:11:14.709
Bruce?

626
01:13:48.487 --> 01:13:50.823
Clear!

627
01:14:00.624 --> 01:14:03.377
- Attention on deck.
- Carry on.

628
01:14:11.385 --> 01:14:14.180
We're buried out here
in the middle of nowhere.

629
01:14:14.305 --> 01:14:16.682
How long are you
gonna keep him sedated?

630
01:14:16.766 --> 01:14:18.976
For the rest of his
natural life. if I have to.

631
01:14:19.018 --> 01:14:21.979
You said I could trust you.
I'm your father.

632
01:14:22.021 --> 01:14:26.317
You can trust me to do what I think
is right. not what you think you want

633
01:14:26.359 --> 01:14:30.404
- He is a human being.
- He is also something else.

634
01:14:30.529 --> 01:14:34.075
Suppose he gets out.
has one of his little mood swings...

635
01:14:34.116 --> 01:14:35.493
in a populated area.

636
01:14:35.576 --> 01:14:40.247
Yes. I'm aware of the potential danger.
I'm also aware that he saved my life.

637
01:14:40.247 --> 01:14:43.250
Yeah. from a mutant
French poodle.

638
01:14:43.334 --> 01:14:45.586
I'm indebted to him for that.

639
01:14:45.670 --> 01:14:49.215
He also put three men in a hospital.
and Talbot's barely walking!

640
01:14:49.298 --> 01:14:53.552
- What do you want me to do?
- I want you to help him!

641
01:14:53.594 --> 01:14:57.431
- Why is he such a threat to you?
- Because I know what he comes from.

642
01:14:57.556 --> 01:15:01.686
He is his father's son.
every last molecule of him.

643
01:15:01.727 --> 01:15:04.313
He says he doesn't know his father

644
01:15:04.355 --> 01:15:09.777
but he's workin'in the same
exact goddamn field his father did.

645
01:15:09.819 --> 01:15:14.156
So either he's lyin'...
or it's somethin' worse. and he's...

646
01:15:14.198 --> 01:15:16.242
What?

647
01:15:16.325 --> 01:15:20.121
Predestined to follow
in his father's footsteps?

648
01:15:21.580 --> 01:15:24.542
I was gonna say "damned."

649
01:15:24.625 --> 01:15:27.128
Of course you were.

650
01:15:27.169 --> 01:15:28.629
But I'm a scientist.

651
01:15:28.713 --> 01:15:33.217
As a scientist. I believe we can figure
this out and he can be helped.

652
01:15:33.259 --> 01:15:36.595
I know you do.

653
01:15:36.637 --> 01:15:40.141
Look. whether you know or care.

654
01:15:40.182 --> 01:15:43.728
I've got a lot of pride
in what you've done.

655
01:15:43.811 --> 01:15:46.814
But this is too big for you.

656
01:15:46.897 --> 01:15:50.860
Look. I know the government thinks
they have a weapon on their hands.

657
01:15:50.943 --> 01:15:53.571
Otherwise. he'd be dead by now.

658
01:15:53.612 --> 01:15:55.990
They can probe and prod
all they want.

659
01:15:56.073 --> 01:15:58.367
and in the meanwhile.
just let me try to help him.

660
01:15:58.451 --> 01:16:01.787
Nobody knows him better than I do

661
01:16:04.665 --> 01:16:07.501
What did David Banner do to him?

662
01:16:11.380 --> 01:16:13.299
Cover left!
Clear left.

663
01:16:13.341 --> 01:16:15.301
Cover right!

664
01:18:25.973 --> 01:18:28.893
What's happening here?

665
01:18:28.893 --> 01:18:31.479
My hand.

666
01:18:32.897 --> 01:18:37.109
You see. the strength
of my son's DNA...

667
01:18:37.193 --> 01:18:41.530
combined with nanomed
reconstruction...

668
01:18:43.991 --> 01:18:47.995
You see. I can partake
with the essences of all things.

669
01:18:49.789 --> 01:18:52.291
Gonna have to ask you to...

670
01:18:52.333 --> 01:18:55.378
put your hands up. pal. okay?

671
01:18:55.461 --> 01:18:58.881
Nice and easy.

672
01:19:03.803 --> 01:19:05.846
Do you really believe...

673
01:19:05.971 --> 01:19:10.643
that I am separate from you?

674
01:19:10.685 --> 01:19:12.978
Whoa!

675
01:19:27.743 --> 01:19:29.745
Where am I?

676
01:19:33.708 --> 01:19:35.668
You're home.

677
01:19:47.972 --> 01:19:50.891
It's hard to believe
we used to live here.

678
01:19:53.519 --> 01:19:56.480
I must have seen you or known you.

679
01:19:56.564 --> 01:19:59.400
If only I could remember.

680
01:20:33.142 --> 01:20:36.062
This is my old house. isn't it?

681
01:21:14.684 --> 01:21:16.769
Let's go.

682
01:21:18.479 --> 01:21:20.439
Please try.

683
01:22:14.618 --> 01:22:16.704
What is it?

684
01:22:16.829 --> 01:22:18.831
Nothing.

685
01:22:18.873 --> 01:22:20.916
Really?

686
01:22:23.252 --> 01:22:25.755
Damn it.

687
01:22:30.384 --> 01:22:34.555
Okay. Betty...
what do you want to know?

688
01:22:37.892 --> 01:22:40.603
What was in that room?

689
01:22:51.489 --> 01:22:54.200
What are you afraid that I'll see?

690
01:22:59.413 --> 01:23:03.250
See? There's nothing.

691
01:23:03.334 --> 01:23:06.545
It's empty.

692
01:23:18.432 --> 01:23:21.227
What do you mean.
I don't have access to him?

693
01:23:21.268 --> 01:23:26.691
NSA has decided to turn over study
of the. uh... the threat to Atheon.

694
01:23:26.732 --> 01:23:29.276
But you're head of the base.

695
01:23:29.318 --> 01:23:31.779
I thought you were in charge.

696
01:23:31.862 --> 01:23:36.492
But I don't set policy.
and I still take orders.

697
01:23:38.869 --> 01:23:42.832
I can't believe Talbot
would go around me like this!

698
01:23:44.250 --> 01:23:47.920
Oh. there's a lot of powerful people
that want in on this.

699
01:23:48.004 --> 01:23:51.298
And money to be made...
lots of it.

700
01:23:56.303 --> 01:23:59.515
You know the worst part
about all this?

701
01:23:59.598 --> 01:24:02.643
When I had David Banner locked up
and sent that kid away.

702
01:24:02.727 --> 01:24:06.939
I didn't give that boy a second thought;
he was just collateral damage.

703
01:24:06.981 --> 01:24:10.192
Well. he isn't anymore. is he?

704
01:24:12.486 --> 01:24:14.447
What can I do?

705
01:24:14.488 --> 01:24:17.992
You can go home now.

706
01:24:19.952 --> 01:24:23.122
I'd tell you to go and say good-bye.
but I've already been informed...

707
01:24:23.247 --> 01:24:27.001
that for now all further contact
is out of the question.

708
01:24:28.377 --> 01:24:29.837
Right.

709
01:25:08.292 --> 01:25:12.755
Hiya. Bruce. How ya feelin'?
Grub okay in here for ya?

710
01:25:12.797 --> 01:25:15.132
What do you want?

711
01:25:15.216 --> 01:25:17.593
That's a good question.

712
01:25:17.635 --> 01:25:22.390
See. I need your cells to trigger
some chemical distress signals.

713
01:25:22.473 --> 01:25:26.310
You know. so you can turn
a little green for me again...

714
01:25:26.394 --> 01:25:29.647
and I can carve off
a piece of the real you.

715
01:25:29.730 --> 01:25:32.692
analyze it. patent it.
make a fortune.

716
01:25:33.943 --> 01:25:36.529
Do you mind?

717
01:25:36.612 --> 01:25:38.823
I'll never let you.

718
01:25:38.906 --> 01:25:41.450
I'm not sure you've got
much of a choice.

719
01:25:43.995 --> 01:25:46.664
Come on. Bruce.
Aren't you feeling a little angry?

720
01:25:46.747 --> 01:25:51.043
After all. you've only got me to play with now
that Betty's dumped you and gone back to Berkeley

721
01:25:51.293 --> 01:25:52.878
You're lying.

722
01:25:52.920 --> 01:25:55.339
You know. for me
this is a win-win situation.

723
01:25:55.464 --> 01:25:57.800
You turn green. and all these guys
come in and kill you...

724
01:25:57.842 --> 01:25:59.677
and I perform the autopsy.

725
01:25:59.719 --> 01:26:02.888
You don't...

726
01:26:02.972 --> 01:26:04.849
And I mop the floor with you...

727
01:26:04.932 --> 01:26:07.893
and maybe by accident
go too far and break your neck.

728
01:26:07.977 --> 01:26:12.231
Bad science. maybe...
but personally gratifying.

729
01:26:14.650 --> 01:26:18.237
Come on. Bruce!
Let's see what you got.

730
01:26:18.321 --> 01:26:20.906
Never.

731
01:26:26.579 --> 01:26:28.873
You know. consciously
you may control it.

732
01:26:28.956 --> 01:26:32.585
but subconsciously.
I bet that's another story.

733
01:27:03.240 --> 01:27:06.327
All right. let's jump-start
those brain waves.

734
01:27:17.421 --> 01:27:19.382
Bruce.

735
01:27:32.395 --> 01:27:34.855
- My dear Miss Ross.

736
01:27:34.897 --> 01:27:36.816
Welcome back.

737
01:27:36.899 --> 01:27:39.568
There are two guards
right outside.

738
01:27:39.652 --> 01:27:44.782
You don't have to worry.
I'm not angry with you. Not anymore.

739
01:27:44.865 --> 01:27:47.118
What do you want?

740
01:27:47.201 --> 01:27:50.413
It's over for me now.
I know that.

741
01:27:50.496 --> 01:27:54.083
And soon it'll be over for Bruce.

742
01:27:54.166 --> 01:27:56.627
That's why I've come to you...

743
01:27:56.711 --> 01:28:00.923
to ask you if you could
persuade your father.

744
01:28:01.007 --> 01:28:03.759
as a man. as a father himself.

745
01:28:03.843 --> 01:28:08.472
that if I turn myself in now.
peacefully...

746
01:28:08.514 --> 01:28:12.101
and before
he puts me away forever.

747
01:28:12.143 --> 01:28:15.021
that he would let me see my son...

748
01:28:15.104 --> 01:28:17.648
for one last time.

749
01:28:17.690 --> 01:28:20.526
Could you do that for me?

750
01:28:23.070 --> 01:28:25.781
It's out of my father's hands now.

751
01:28:30.453 --> 01:28:33.748
I understand.
He's a puppet now.

752
01:28:35.041 --> 01:28:37.376
I don't blame him.
You shouldn't.

753
01:28:37.418 --> 01:28:41.172
You should blame yourself
for what you've done to your son.

754
01:28:41.255 --> 01:28:44.967
And what have I done
to my son. Miss Ross?

755
01:28:45.051 --> 01:28:50.389
Nothing. I tried to improve
on the limits in myself.

756
01:28:50.473 --> 01:28:52.808
Myself! Not him!

757
01:28:52.850 --> 01:28:56.437
Can you understand?
To improve on nature.

758
01:28:56.520 --> 01:28:59.482
My nature!
Knowledge of oneself!

759
01:28:59.565 --> 01:29:02.526
It's the only path to the truth...

760
01:29:02.526 --> 01:29:06.614
that give men the power
to go beyond God's boundaries!

761
01:29:07.615 --> 01:29:12.036
You know what's beyond
your boundaries? Other people.

762
01:29:12.119 --> 01:29:15.164
All you've given Bruce is fear.

763
01:29:17.500 --> 01:29:20.211
Fear of life.

764
01:29:22.380 --> 01:29:24.298
Fear?

765
01:29:25.716 --> 01:29:27.677
Perhaps. Miss Ross.

766
01:29:29.720 --> 01:29:32.139
And loneliness too.

767
01:29:32.181 --> 01:29:37.019
Yes... I feel them both.

768
01:29:40.564 --> 01:29:45.403
But I have lived...
completely once.

769
01:29:47.738 --> 01:29:50.408
I was so much in love.

770
01:29:50.449 --> 01:29:53.452
and she so much wanted a baby.

771
01:29:53.494 --> 01:29:55.454
My baby.

772
01:30:03.129 --> 01:30:05.965
I could tell
from the moment she conceived...

773
01:30:06.090 --> 01:30:09.051
that it wasn't a son
I had given her...

774
01:30:09.176 --> 01:30:11.429
but something else.

775
01:30:11.512 --> 01:30:13.889
A monster. maybe.

776
01:30:13.931 --> 01:30:16.726
I should have put a stop to it
right then.

777
01:30:16.809 --> 01:30:21.230
but I was curious
and that was my downfall.

778
01:30:21.355 --> 01:30:25.276
And as I watched this tiny life unfold.

779
01:30:25.443 --> 01:30:28.654
I began to imagine the horror of it.

780
01:30:28.738 --> 01:30:33.034
and my curiosity was replaced...

781
01:30:33.117 --> 01:30:36.120
with compassion.

782
01:30:38.456 --> 01:30:41.125
But they took away
my chance to cure him.

783
01:30:41.208 --> 01:30:43.502
Your father threw me out.

784
01:30:43.586 --> 01:30:47.089
- What are you doing?
- I remember that day so well...

785
01:30:47.173 --> 01:30:49.967
every moment. every sensation...

786
01:30:50.051 --> 01:30:52.303
walking into the house.

787
01:30:52.386 --> 01:30:55.598
the feeling of the handle
of the knife in my hand.

788
01:30:55.639 --> 01:31:00.686
I knew I was doing a father's work.
fulfilling a father's mercy.

789
01:31:00.686 --> 01:31:03.773
David. please stop it! No!

790
01:31:03.856 --> 01:31:06.317
David. no!
Talk to me! Listen!

791
01:31:06.400 --> 01:31:09.320
But then she surprised me.

792
01:31:09.362 --> 01:31:13.115
- No! No!

793
01:31:13.199 --> 01:31:15.242
David. no!

794
01:31:15.284 --> 01:31:18.496
It was as if...

795
01:31:18.621 --> 01:31:21.999
she and the knife...

796
01:31:22.083 --> 01:31:24.752
merged.

797
01:31:33.386 --> 01:31:35.554
No!

798
01:31:35.638 --> 01:31:38.349
You cannot imagine...

799
01:31:38.432 --> 01:31:42.061
the unbearable finality of it.

800
01:31:42.144 --> 01:31:45.606
And in that one moment...

801
01:31:45.648 --> 01:31:49.902
I took everything that was dear to me...

802
01:31:49.986 --> 01:31:54.323
and transformed it into nothing more...

803
01:31:54.407 --> 01:31:56.409
than a memory.

804
01:32:11.799 --> 01:32:15.136
Bingo! That must be some
jumbo nightmare he just had.

805
01:32:19.807 --> 01:32:22.018
Okay. do it now.
Start the enzyme extraction.

806
01:32:26.772 --> 01:32:29.108
Sir. negative on drill penetration.

807
01:32:29.191 --> 01:32:32.903
Damn it. drill him harder! Give him full RPMs
Come on. Holeman! Come on!

808
01:32:46.959 --> 01:32:51.464
-Should I neutralize?
-No. I can't do anything with goop. c'mon on

809
01:33:03.601 --> 01:33:06.771
- All right. put him to sleep.

810
01:33:15.696 --> 01:33:17.990
It's not stopping him!

811
01:33:25.122 --> 01:33:27.583
Ready room. send in
our containment team.

812
01:33:27.667 --> 01:33:30.419
Non-lethals only.
I repeat. non-lethals only.

813
01:33:30.503 --> 01:33:32.713
I must have a sample of him.

814
01:33:32.797 --> 01:33:34.715
Sir!

815
01:33:36.384 --> 01:33:39.887
- Jesus!
- Hit him with the foam.

816
01:33:39.929 --> 01:33:41.847
Deploy containment foam.

817
01:33:42.932 --> 01:33:44.892
Talbot. talk to me.

818
01:33:46.477 --> 01:33:49.897
Under control. General. I'll let
you know if we need you.

819
01:33:49.939 --> 01:33:52.608
Unacceptable.  Unseat your
asses down here immediately.

820
01:33:52.650 --> 01:33:54.777
I want a full-court evacuation now.

821
01:33:54.860 --> 01:33:57.279
I'm shutting you down.
Lockdown.

822
01:33:57.279 --> 01:34:00.116
-Didn't you hear what the general said?
-I said lockdown!

823
01:34:02.827 --> 01:34:05.287
Clear! I need a sample of him!

824
01:34:07.289 --> 01:34:10.626
Take it easy there. buddy.

825
01:34:10.751 --> 01:34:14.547
This might give you
a bit of a sting here. Bruce.

826
01:34:26.684 --> 01:34:30.021
- Fall back! Fall back!
- Clear your weapon! Clear it!

827
01:34:30.104 --> 01:34:33.691
- Give me the M2.
- So long. big boy.

828
01:34:33.774 --> 01:34:36.152
Clear!

829
01:34:46.037 --> 01:34:49.165
Lockdown the entire facility immediately

830
01:34:53.377 --> 01:34:56.380
Target's still moving towards blue level

831
01:34:56.464 --> 01:34:59.717
- Evacuate the main hall.

832
01:35:04.055 --> 01:35:07.683
Send in backup. heavy weapons.
Issue general quarters.

833
01:35:07.725 --> 01:35:10.478
Set firing lines left and right!

834
01:35:10.478 --> 01:35:13.230
Heavy weapons. go. go. go!

835
01:35:35.044 --> 01:35:37.213
Contamination. sir.
System readings are redline.

836
01:35:37.254 --> 01:35:39.465
Data's on backup power supply.

837
01:35:46.430 --> 01:35:48.599
Incoming!

838
01:35:55.356 --> 01:35:58.067
-Shut down all power to the main hall
-Sir?

839
01:35:58.109 --> 01:36:02.738
Show him the way out.
We'll fight him outside.

840
01:38:11.283 --> 01:38:14.370
Driver. stop.
Driver. stop.

841
01:38:21.377 --> 01:38:23.879
Gunner. traverse left!
Traverse left!

842
01:39:06.547 --> 01:39:08.466
Clear back! Clear back!

843
01:40:02.645 --> 01:40:06.857
Mr. President.
I have some bad news. sir.

844
01:40:06.941 --> 01:40:08.901
Let's have it. General.

845
01:40:09.026 --> 01:40:12.196
I've briefed the president on Angry Man.
I assume that's what this is about.

846
01:40:12.238 --> 01:40:16.993
It is. ma'am. I'm requesting
a National Command Authority override.

847
01:40:17.034 --> 01:40:19.870
Angry Man is unsecure.

848
01:40:19.912 --> 01:40:24.291
I need everything we have at my disposal
in order to stop his movement.

849
01:40:24.417 --> 01:40:27.920
You're expecting
civilian casualties. General?

850
01:40:28.004 --> 01:40:30.256
Not if I can help it. ma'am.

851
01:40:30.339 --> 01:40:32.591
Consider it done.  Keep us posted.

852
01:41:21.182 --> 01:41:23.100
Contact Goodman Control.

853
01:41:23.184 --> 01:41:25.686
Patch data to the assets.

854
01:41:25.770 --> 01:41:28.606
Contact H.Q.

855
01:41:28.648 --> 01:41:32.443
Have them initiate
an immediate evacuation...

856
01:41:32.526 --> 01:41:37.698
in vicinity of grid coordinates
653-216...

857
01:42:11.816 --> 01:42:13.985
Confirm that the area
has been cleared.

858
01:42:14.068 --> 01:42:16.570
Confirm area cleared.

859
01:42:16.612 --> 01:42:19.532
H.Q. Confirms area cleared.
Assets on-line. sir.

860
01:42:19.573 --> 01:42:21.867
Gentlemen. it's time to dig in.

861
01:42:21.951 --> 01:42:25.371
I want this target
stopped in his tracks.

862
01:43:15.004 --> 01:43:16.922
Jesus.

863
01:43:32.104 --> 01:43:35.566
Mayday! Mayday! Ah. shit!

864
01:43:41.447 --> 01:43:45.618
Tango Four is down. Have C-SAR
respond to our 20 ASAP.

865
01:43:45.701 --> 01:43:49.872
We're okay. but. damn it. get him
off us before he tears us apart!

866
01:43:49.955 --> 01:43:52.625
I've got no shot.
Do you have a clear line of fire?

867
01:43:52.708 --> 01:43:54.960
Watch it. Tango Flight.

868
01:43:54.960 --> 01:43:57.380
Break left! Break left!

869
01:43:57.421 --> 01:44:00.925
Tango Three. pull back and set up
for a Hellfire shot.

870
01:44:00.966 --> 01:44:03.427
Hold your fire till we draw him off.

871
01:44:03.511 --> 01:44:05.805
Tango One is hot. Gun wazzed.

872
01:44:05.888 --> 01:44:08.474
Roger. Going hot. Guns ready.

873
01:44:12.478 --> 01:44:16.607
Engage at will.

874
01:44:35.751 --> 01:44:38.754
Tango One. pull back!
Clear my line!

875
01:44:38.754 --> 01:44:41.757
Tango Flight. clear back.
I've got him painted for Hellfire.

876
01:44:41.799 --> 01:44:46.345
Roger that. Tango One clear.
Take the shot.

877
01:45:04.572 --> 01:45:07.700
Tango One. Tango Three.
I have contact.

878
01:45:07.742 --> 01:45:10.244
Holy shit! He's got my missile!

879
01:45:12.163 --> 01:45:14.165
Mayday! Mayday!

880
01:45:16.667 --> 01:45:20.171
Mayday! Mayday!
We're hit! We're going down!

881
01:45:23.090 --> 01:45:25.468
Give me a head count.

882
01:45:25.509 --> 01:45:28.721
Tango Three. give me a sit rep.

883
01:45:28.804 --> 01:45:32.516
Our kite's busted up.
but we're okay.

884
01:45:32.558 --> 01:45:36.145
Tango Flight. do you have
eyes on the target?

885
01:45:36.187 --> 01:45:39.315
Tango One. I have him in the rocks.

886
01:45:39.357 --> 01:45:42.443
Salvo all. Turn it into a parking lot.

887
01:46:02.797 --> 01:46:05.424
T-bolt. your parking lot is ready.

888
01:46:05.424 --> 01:46:08.219
We're bingo for fuel and ammo.
R. T.B.

889
01:46:35.204 --> 01:46:37.373
T-bolt. this is Goodman Control.

890
01:46:37.456 --> 01:46:41.127
Be advised. target not destroyed.
He's on the move again.

891
01:46:41.127 --> 01:46:43.087
Damn!

892
01:46:43.129 --> 01:46:45.589
I've got it.

893
01:46:45.631 --> 01:46:47.800
It appears he's heading home.

894
01:46:47.883 --> 01:46:49.802
Launch fast movers.

895
01:46:49.885 --> 01:46:53.514
Have them intercept and engage.

896
01:46:53.597 --> 01:46:55.766
Hello?

897
01:46:55.808 --> 01:46:59.478
Betty. Bruce got out.
He's headed your way...

898
01:46:59.562 --> 01:47:01.272
and probably right for you.

899
01:47:01.355 --> 01:47:03.649
How far from the base are you?

900
01:47:03.733 --> 01:47:06.861
I'm already here.
They're taking his father in now.

901
01:47:06.944 --> 01:47:10.698
That's all good news.
Stay there. Betty.

902
01:47:24.628 --> 01:47:27.548
Legend One rolling in hot.
Legend Two breaking offleft.

903
01:47:27.631 --> 01:47:31.719
I think I can come back around
for a gun attack.

904
01:47:31.761 --> 01:47:35.097
Acquire a clear target.
Fire at will.

905
01:47:39.477 --> 01:47:43.356
Increase altitude.
Civilian aircraft in vicinity.

906
01:47:47.193 --> 01:47:50.738
Pull up! Pull up!
You're headed for the bridge!

907
01:47:50.821 --> 01:47:54.867
I can't pull up! I can't pull up!

908
01:48:03.042 --> 01:48:06.337
Okay. you've got him now. Take him
on a ride to the top of the world.

909
01:48:06.420 --> 01:48:09.340
Let's see what the thin air
will do for him.

910
01:48:09.423 --> 01:48:11.509
Initiating afterburner.

911
01:48:29.068 --> 01:48:31.112
I'm passing flight level 600.

912
01:48:31.195 --> 01:48:33.406
This is out of my envelope.

913
01:48:33.489 --> 01:48:35.449
Hang in there. Legend.

914
01:48:35.574 --> 01:48:38.995
I can't maintain.
He's all over my aerodynamics.

915
01:48:39.036 --> 01:48:41.247
He'll lose consciousness before you.

916
01:48:44.917 --> 01:48:50.464
Nine-fifty. I can't hold it.
I'm pulling back!

917
01:49:36.886 --> 01:49:39.388
Puny human.

918
01:49:49.482 --> 01:49:51.442
Contact. He's in the water.
All units. weapons hot.

919
01:49:51.525 --> 01:49:53.903
Let's not take any chances.

920
01:49:53.986 --> 01:49:57.406
You are cleared to fire
on target. Legend.

921
01:50:18.427 --> 01:50:20.471
- Dad?
- Betty?

922
01:50:20.554 --> 01:50:22.974
We don't have a choice.

923
01:50:23.099 --> 01:50:25.434
I have to destroy him.

924
01:50:25.518 --> 01:50:29.605
But you can't.  You will only fuel
his rage. and you will make him stronger

925
01:50:29.689 --> 01:50:34.110
It's you he's coming for.
You know that.

926
01:50:35.277 --> 01:50:37.822
Then let me go to him.

927
01:50:37.863 --> 01:50:39.865
Please.

928
01:50:41.325 --> 01:50:44.078
Just give him a chance to calm down

929
01:51:08.561 --> 01:51:12.398
This area has been declared
restricted airspace.

930
01:51:12.481 --> 01:51:16.319
All aircraft are ordered
to clear the airspace immediately.

931
01:51:57.360 --> 01:51:59.945
Echo. One-niner. Weapons are hot.

932
01:52:00.029 --> 01:52:02.573
Target acquired.
Waiting your orders to engage.

933
01:52:02.615 --> 01:52:05.368
Repeat. waiting
your orders to engage.

934
01:52:05.451 --> 01:52:08.788
Command code yellow.
Hold for authorization.

935
01:52:18.255 --> 01:52:20.257
All units. hold your fire.

936
01:52:20.341 --> 01:52:23.719
This is T-bolt to all assets. You have
direct orders to hold your fire.

937
01:52:23.844 --> 01:52:26.305
I repeat. hold your fire.

938
01:52:26.389 --> 01:52:28.641
Echo. One-niner. Roger that.

939
01:52:42.780 --> 01:52:44.782
Go go. go. go. go. go!

940
01:53:14.812 --> 01:53:17.773
Hold your fire until my command!

941
01:53:20.318 --> 01:53:22.862
Engine 24 to command.
We are in position now.

942
01:54:30.221 --> 01:54:32.848
You found me.

943
01:54:34.225 --> 01:54:37.061
You weren't that hard to find.

944
01:54:38.646 --> 01:54:40.648
Yes. I was.

945
01:55:46.130 --> 01:55:48.090
Let's take a walk.

946
01:56:19.789 --> 01:56:23.084
That's the deal. gentlemen.
He stays on this base...

947
01:56:23.167 --> 01:56:27.546
until we get the final word from C-3
on how to dispose of him.

948
01:56:27.588 --> 01:56:32.510
In the meantime. ifhe does
anything but sit there in that chair.

949
01:56:32.635 --> 01:56:37.515
we're gonna turn on the juice
and he'll be incinerated immediately.

950
01:56:37.598 --> 01:56:40.017
We've established a
200-yard perimeter. sir.

951
01:56:40.101 --> 01:56:44.355
If we deploy the electromagnetic array.
there should be no collateral damage.

952
01:56:44.438 --> 01:56:47.274
Here they come!

953
01:56:53.364 --> 01:56:55.825
I'm doin' this for you. Betty.

954
01:56:55.908 --> 01:56:59.870
But one way or another. we're
gonna have to prepare for the worst.

955
01:58:49.146 --> 01:58:51.232
I should have killed you.

956
01:58:52.400 --> 01:58:54.986
And I should have killed you.

957
01:58:56.195 --> 01:58:58.572
I wish you had.

958
01:59:03.244 --> 01:59:05.621
I saw her last night.

959
01:59:07.790 --> 01:59:10.209
Saw her face.

960
01:59:10.251 --> 01:59:12.378
Brown hair.

961
01:59:14.171 --> 01:59:16.674
Brown eyes.

962
01:59:16.757 --> 01:59:19.593
She smiled at me.

963
01:59:19.677 --> 01:59:23.389
She reached down and kissed my cheek

964
01:59:24.724 --> 01:59:28.019
I can almost remember a smell.

965
01:59:31.188 --> 01:59:34.191
Almost like desert flowers.

966
01:59:35.693 --> 01:59:37.778
Her favorite perfume.

967
01:59:40.614 --> 01:59:44.744
It's my mother.
and I don't even know her name.

968
01:59:52.710 --> 01:59:56.505
It's all right. son.
You go ahead and cry.

969
02:00:03.638 --> 02:00:06.432
Go ahead and cry.

970
02:00:09.352 --> 02:00:11.812
Cry. Crying will do you good.

971
02:00:11.979 --> 02:00:14.732
Don't touch me!

972
02:00:16.150 --> 02:00:18.944
Maybe once you were my father.

973
02:00:18.986 --> 02:00:21.739
but you're not now
and you never will be.

974
02:00:21.822 --> 02:00:25.368
Oh. is that so?

975
02:00:25.451 --> 02:00:31.123
Well. I got news for you.
I didn't come here to see you.

976
02:00:31.207 --> 02:00:34.293
I came here to see my son.

977
02:00:35.628 --> 02:00:37.755
My real son.

978
02:00:37.838 --> 02:00:40.341
The one inside of you.

979
02:00:40.383 --> 02:00:44.470
You're nothing but a superficial shell.

980
02:00:44.595 --> 02:00:46.722
a husk of flimsy consciousness...

981
02:00:46.806 --> 02:00:50.726
ready to be torn off
at a moment's notice.

982
02:00:50.768 --> 02:00:54.146
You can think what you like.
I don't care. Just go!

983
02:00:59.694 --> 02:01:03.155
No. son. Listen to me.
I found a cure.

984
02:01:03.239 --> 02:01:05.574
For me.

985
02:01:05.658 --> 02:01:08.911
My cells can transform too.

986
02:01:08.911 --> 02:01:11.831
absorb enormous amounts of energy.

987
02:01:11.956 --> 02:01:14.750
But. unlike you. they're unstable.

988
02:01:14.834 --> 02:01:18.087
Son. I need your strength.

989
02:01:18.170 --> 02:01:21.424
I gave you life.

990
02:01:21.549 --> 02:01:25.428
Now you must give it back to me!

991
02:01:25.469 --> 02:01:30.683
Only a million times
more radiant. more powerful!

992
02:01:30.766 --> 02:01:34.145
- Stop it.
- Stop? Stop what?

993
02:01:34.228 --> 02:01:36.981
Stop what?

994
02:01:37.064 --> 02:01:41.360
Think about all those men out there
in their uniforms...

995
02:01:41.485 --> 02:01:44.947
barking and swallowing orders.

996
02:01:45.031 --> 02:01:48.409
inflicting their petty rule
over the entire globe!

997
02:01:48.492 --> 02:01:51.704
Think of all the harm they've done!

998
02:01:51.787 --> 02:01:54.790
To you! To me!

999
02:01:54.874 --> 02:01:57.126
To humanity!

1000
02:01:57.251 --> 02:02:00.212
And know this...
that we can make them...

1001
02:02:00.296 --> 02:02:02.882
and their flags and their anthems
and their governments...

1002
02:02:02.923 --> 02:02:05.635
disappear in a flash!

1003
02:02:05.676 --> 02:02:07.845
You in me.

1004
02:02:07.887 --> 02:02:10.139
I'd rather die.

1005
02:02:10.264 --> 02:02:14.769
Oh. that's your answer?

1006
02:02:14.852 --> 02:02:19.148
Then indeed you shall die...
and be reborn...

1007
02:02:19.231 --> 02:02:22.652
a hero... of the kind
that walked the earth...

1008
02:02:22.735 --> 02:02:26.447
long before the pale religions
of civilization...

1009
02:02:26.530 --> 02:02:29.784
infected humanity's soul!

1010
02:02:29.867 --> 02:02:32.995
Go!

1011
02:02:46.467 --> 02:02:49.387
Stop your bawling.

1012
02:02:49.428 --> 02:02:52.848
you weak little speck
of human trash.

1013
02:02:59.313 --> 02:03:02.233
All right... I'll go!

1014
02:03:03.985 --> 02:03:06.654
- You just watch me go!
- Hit it.

1015
02:03:31.304 --> 02:03:34.390
- Hit it again!

1016
02:03:34.473 --> 02:03:38.269
We can't. sir. There's no power. Some
kind of counter-electromagnetic field.

1017
02:03:42.940 --> 02:03:45.401
Move in and assault the target.
Move in!

1018
02:03:45.484 --> 02:03:48.779
Move. move. move!

1019
02:04:37.161 --> 02:04:40.748
Sir. I've located them on radar.
Pear Lake.

1020
02:04:40.831 --> 02:04:43.209
Call up the task force.

1021
02:04:49.882 --> 02:04:52.218
Yes!

1022
02:05:56.657 --> 02:05:59.535
That's right. Keep fighting.

1023
02:05:59.618 --> 02:06:04.165
The more you fight.
the more of you I take.

1024
02:06:11.714 --> 02:06:16.677
Strange. We're reading a phenomenal
drop in temperatures there.

1025
02:06:16.719 --> 02:06:19.263
But simultaneous radiological activity.

1026
02:06:19.388 --> 02:06:22.558
They're absorbing
all the ambient energy.

1027
02:06:31.901 --> 02:06:36.072
Sleep now. Bruce. and forget forever.

1028
02:06:36.113 --> 02:06:41.077
Struggle no more...
and give me all of your power.

1029
02:06:42.912 --> 02:06:46.916
You think you can live with it? Take it!

1030
02:06:46.999 --> 02:06:50.670
Take it all!

1031
02:06:52.380 --> 02:06:55.800
Oh. yes! Yes!

1032
02:07:09.230 --> 02:07:12.608
Take it back!

1033
02:07:12.650 --> 02:07:16.487
It's not stopping!

1034
02:07:16.570 --> 02:07:18.823
Take it back!

1035
02:07:34.964 --> 02:07:37.717
Gentlemen... release.

1036
02:07:46.142 --> 02:07:49.145
Gamma charge away.

1037
02:08:10.583 --> 02:08:14.003
- Mwah!
- Sweet dreams.

1038
